<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pietak-bioelectric-morphogen-coupling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Pietak & Levin (2017) electrodiffusive Nernst-Planck gap-junction morphogen transport & cryptic two-headed memory — MorphoEval overall 58.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 baseline assessment of `2017-pietak-bioelectric-morphogen-coupling.py` (58.6/100). The initial Nernst-Planck solver captures electrodiffusive drift of cationic serotonin (5-HT, z=+1) toward the hyperpolarized posterior wound and basic wild-type 1H1T vs 8-octanol 2H0T switching, but requires Scharfetter-Gummel Bernoulli flux discretization to reach exact Boltzmann equilibrium (c_post/c_ant = exp(40/25.85) = 4.7002), explicit simulation of cryptic two-headed (`2H0T`) memory persistence after transient 8-octanol washout plus bioelectric K+ hyperpolarization rescue (`1H1T`) and neutral valence (`z=0`) ablation control, and automated bilateral photoreceptor ocelli segmentation on `planarian_ap_polarity_specimen.jpg`. Overall 58.1/100 (faithfulness 56.2, reproducibility 62.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 62, Morphological realism / specimen match 52, Parameter expressivity 57, Morphometric validation 55, Source and data traceability 66, Code-to-model traceability 60, Reproducibility package 61. Output judged: docs/media/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling_comparison.png: rendered output of 2017-pietak-bioelectric-morphogen-coupling.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 556422 B, 2268×1863 px, artifact_sha256 13866bfc1f2741223e1a9f254b38f8424907b00fb5e328dc4576f885fdb242dc (sha256 13866bfc1f2741223e1a9f254b38f8424907b00fb5e328dc4576f885fdb242dc), spec_fingerprint d43466962273a22db00389bf276a7fa5ef9addd555b89cf3850d949e0d0823ee. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d43466962273a22db00389bf276a7fa5ef9addd555b89cf3850d949e0d0823ee; artifact_sha256: 13866bfc1f2741223e1a9f254b38f8424907b00fb5e328dc4576f885fdb242dc; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling_reference.json=b118960086d59e02..., datasets/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling/paper_citations.bib=c446e775222f552c..., datasets/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling/planarian_ap_polarity_specimen.jpg=466029cc05610678..., datasets/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling/scout_manifest.json=bc8a4a2c8e734e1d...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add automated Gaussian local-contrast ocelli (eyespot) detection and 60-bin dorsoventral width segmentation on `datasets/bioelectric_morphogen_coupling/planarian_ap_polarity_specimen.jpg`, plus 2D body-plan contour synthesis for 1H1T, cryptic 2H0T, and 0H2T regenerates.",
        "remediation needed: Implement conservative Scharfetter-Gummel Bernoulli flux discretization for Nernst-Planck gap-junction transport so the 1D PDE converges to the exact Boltzmann equilibrium ratio c_post/c_ant = exp(-z*(V_post - V_ant)/V_T) = 4.7002.",
        "remediation needed: Simulate all 6 canonical regimes including transient 8-octanol washout cryptic two-headed (`2H0T`) memory persistence, neutral morphogen valence (`z=0`) ablation control, and posterior K+ hyperpolarization bioelectric rescue (`1H1T`)." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.81e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pietak-bioelectric-morphogen-coupling-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
